{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_lskemhv6jifzomisbkyqwdh42saf7o623yifpidv2oyh7zufbleq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01RW2jZ1arAWrCbWDcmJt1NL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='ERRORS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold = \"| 31 | `print_item` / `print_order` / `find_items_by_category` | fixed-size buffer with no NUL in it | `printf(\\\"%s\\\")` / `strcmp` read past the field (UB) | UB, note B |\"\nnew = \"| 31 | `print_item` / `print_order` / `find_items_by_category` | fixed-size buffer with no NUL in it | `printf(\\\"%s\\\")` / `strcmp` keep reading past the field, into the bytes that follow | `[x]` `errors::unterminated_fields_read_into_the_next_field` (within-struct part; see note B) |\"\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, new)\n\nold_b = \"\"\"**B. Deliberately unchecked reads.** Row 31: `item_t.name` /\n`item_t.category` / `order_t.customer_name` are always NUL-terminated when the\nstruct comes from `create_item`/`create_order` (C forces\n`buf[MAX-1] = '\\\\0'`). A hand-built struct with no NUL makes C's `printf(\"%s\")`\nand `strcmp` walk into the following fields — undefined behaviour with no\ndeterministic result, so the tests do not assert a byte-for-byte result for it;\nthe Rust translation instead stops at the end of the field. Every tested struct\nis built through `create_item`/`create_order`, exactly like the C program does.\"\"\"\nnew_b = \"\"\"**B. Unterminated fields.** Row 31: `item_t.name` / `item_t.category` /\n`order_t.customer_name` are always NUL-terminated when the struct comes from\n`create_item`/`create_order` (C forces `buf[MAX-1] = '\\\\0'`). A hand-built struct\nwith no NUL makes C's `printf(\"%s\")` and `strcmp` walk into the following bytes.\nThe Rust translation reproduces that: `%s` is emitted with an unbounded read from\nthe field's address (`cio::c_str_ptr`), and `strcmp` is a raw byte loop, so the\nwalk continues into `category`/the padding/`price` exactly as in C. The test\nbuilds `item_t`/`order_t` from all 120 / 80 raw bytes (padding included) and\nplaces the terminating NUL in a *later field*, which makes the walk deterministic\nand lets it be compared byte for byte. Where the walk would leave the struct\nentirely, the bytes are the callee's stack and no implementation-independent\nresult exists, so that sub-case is deliberately not asserted.\"\"\"\nassert old_b in s\ns = s.replace(old_b, new_b)\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"Legend for \"tested\": `[x]` = differential test passes against both `.so`s;\n`UB` = the C code has no check and the behaviour is undefined (dereferencing\nNULL / reading out of bounds), so the row is asserted only as far as it is\ndeterministic — see the notes at the bottom.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Legend for \"tested\": `[x]` = a differential test constructs the condition and\nasserts that both `.so`s return the same sentinel / print the same bytes / die\nfrom the same signal. Every row below is `[x]`. Rows whose C behaviour is\nundefined (NULL dereference, reading past a field) are asserted as far as they\nare deterministic, which the notes at the bottom spell out.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(s.count('| `[x]`'), 'rows marked, remaining unmarked:', [l.split('|')[1].strip() for l in s.splitlines() if l.startswith('| ') and l.count('|')>4 and '[x]' not in l and l.split('|')[1].strip().isdigit()])\nPY","description":"Mark ERRORS.md row 31 as tested"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2006,"cache_read_input_tokens":312978,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2006,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d399b7ab-efa0-48e3-8602-3102beab604c","uuid":"ac35b226-621e-441f-a0b9-6cd5dfd6a271","timestamp":"2026-08-19T20:56:37.652Z"}
