{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_qihup7aftzklyklckjzselozdnx65wd6gzutzfd3bcuzn5llenma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01QJjdaXHwnwab45JWP3XpbN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"rm -f Cargo.toml.bak && cat > VERIFICATION.md <<'EOF'\n# VERIFICATION.md — what was verified, what was found, how to re-run\n\nThe C sources in `c_src/` are the ground truth; the Rust crate must produce\nbyte-identical results. Everything below is reproducible with:\n\n```sh\n./run_all.sh            # debug + release, every feature combination\n./run_all.sh debug      # one profile\n```\n\n`run_all.sh` enumerates the build configurations from `Cargo.toml`, `cargo\ncheck`s each, builds the Rust `cdylib` + binary, diffs the exported symbol sets\nof the two shared libraries, and runs the whole differential suite once per\nconfiguration.\n\n## Result\n\n| gate | status |\n|------|--------|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` diff, C `.so` vs Rust `.so` | **63 / 63 symbols, 0 missing, 0 extra, 0 undefined non-libc** |\n| Phase B — every row of `CONFIGS.md` (51 rows) | **all pass**, randomized inputs with fixed seeds |\n| Phase C — every row of `ERRORS.md` (39 rows) | **all pass**, same sentinel / bytes / fatal signal |\n| every build configuration | **default, `--no-default-features`, `--all-features` × debug and release** |\n| total tests | **71**, all green in both profiles |\n\n## How the two implementations are compared\n\n* `build.rs` compiles `c_src/src/main.c` + `c_src/src/inventory.c` (nothing in\n  `c_src/` is modified) into `$OUT_DIR/libdriver_c.so` and `$OUT_DIR/driver_c`.\n* The Rust crate builds as `crate-type = [\"cdylib\", \"rlib\"]`, and `src/capi.rs`\n  exports one `#[no_mangle] extern \"C\"` entry point per C symbol — including the\n  48 names generated by `DEFINE_ARRAY`/`DEFINE_LIST`, and `main`.\n* Every test loads **both** `.so`s with `libloading` and calls only their\n  exported symbols; the Rust functions are never called directly, so the export\n  wrappers and the C ABI (structs by value, `size_t`, `double`, `char *`) are\n  part of what is tested.\n* `printf` output is compared by redirecting file descriptor 1 into a file around\n  each call (C's `stdout` is flushed on both sides), so comparisons are exact\n  byte sequences.\n* Containers are compared *structurally*: `size`, `capacity`, the `data`\n  pointer's contents, and the whole linked-list chain including `head`/`tail`.\n  Because the Rust containers are `#[repr(C)]` and use the same libc\n  `malloc`/`realloc`/`free`, containers cross the library boundary in the tests\n  (C-built container → Rust entry point and vice versa).\n\n## What had to change in the translation\n\n1. **The library had no C ABI at all.** The original translation exposed the\n   program only as a Rust binary with private modules (`Vec`-based containers), so\n   the Rust `.so` exported none of the C `.so`'s 63 symbols. `src/capi.rs` was\n   added, and `src/generic_containers.rs` was re-translated from the\n   `DEFINE_ARRAY`/`DEFINE_LIST` macro bodies as raw-pointer, `malloc`-backed,\n   `#[repr(C)]` containers so that the exported functions are interchangeable with\n   the C ones (`array_TYPE_get`'s unchecked read, `capacity` doubling, the\n   `size_t` multiplication wrap-around, `realloc` failure returning `-1`, …).\n   `main.c`'s `print_menu`/`demo_*`/`main` moved into `src/demos.rs` so they can be\n   exported too; `src/main.rs` is now a thin binary that compiles the same modules\n   and calls `demos::c_main`.\n2. **NaN sign propagation in the accumulators** (found by the randomized Phase B\n   rows, release profile only). `total_value += price * quantity` and\n   `total_revenue += amount` can add two NaNs; x86-64 `ADDSD` keeps the\n   destination operand, which in the unoptimized C build is the *added* value, so\n   C prints the last NaN of the sum. LLVM swaps the commutative operands when\n   optimizing, so a release build printed `$-nan` where C prints `$nan`.\n   `cio::fadd_c` now resolves the NaN cases explicitly. Covered exhaustively by\n   `inventory_stats_nan_inf_exhaustive`, `order_stats_nan_inf_exhaustive` and\n   `stats_nan_positions_in_long_sums`.\n3. **`%f` specials.** `printf(\"%.2f\")` prints `nan`, `-nan`, `inf`, `-inf`, where\n   Rust's `{:.2}` prints `NaN` and drops the NaN sign. `cio::fmt_f` handles the\n   non-finite cases and defers to Rust's exact-and-ties-to-even formatting for\n   finite values (verified against 30 000+ random bit patterns).\n4. **Unchecked dereferences must fault, not panic.** A plain Rust deref of a NULL\n   raw pointer trips the compiler's debug-only null-pointer assertion and aborts\n   (`SIGABRT`), while C faults (`SIGSEGV`). The unchecked reads C performs\n   (`array_TYPE_get`, `strncpy`, `strcmp`, `printf(\"%s\")`) now go through\n   `read_volatile`, so both implementations die from the same signal — asserted in\n   forked children by `errors::ub_null_deref_matches`.\n5. **`%s` is an unbounded read.** `printf(\"%s\", item.name)` walks past a\n   fixed-size field that contains no NUL; `cio::c_str_ptr` reproduces that, so\n   `errors::unterminated_fields_read_into_the_next_field` can compare that walk\n   byte for byte (structs are built from raw bytes, padding included, with the\n   terminating NUL in a later field).\n6. **`int` overflow** in `total_items += item.quantity` wraps\n   (`wrapping_add`), matching the unoptimized C build; covered by\n   `stats_quantity_overflow`.\n\n## Test map\n\n| file | scope |\n|------|-------|\n| `tests/containers.rs` | rows B1–B17: `array_*`/`list_*` for `int`, `double`, `item_t`, `order_t` — capacities, growth ladder, `clear`/reuse, interleaved append/prepend, 500-op random scripts, cross-library interop |\n| `tests/inventory_funcs.rs` | rows B18–B35: `create_item`/`create_order` (string shapes and truncation), `print_item`/`print_order` (30 000+ random doubles), both statistics functions (signs, NaN/inf, division by zero, `int` overflow), both search functions |\n| `tests/demos.rs` | rows B36–B42: `print_menu` and the five `demo_*` functions, individually, repeated, and in random sequences |\n| `tests/driver_e2e.rs` | rows B43–B47: the exported `main` of each `.so` in a forked child, plus the two executables, over 46 hand-derived stdin shapes and 60 random sessions |\n| `tests/errors.rs` | all 39 `ERRORS.md` rows, including `malloc`/`realloc` failure (heap exhausted under `RLIMIT_AS` in a forked child), NULL arguments, empty containers, unterminated fields, and matching fatal signals |\n| `tests/symbols.rs` | Phase D inside the suite: `nm -D` set equality both ways, `dlsym` for all 63 names, and the documented symbol set |\n\n## Note on running the tests\n\nThe output comparison redirects file descriptor 1, which is process-global, so\nthe tests must not run concurrently. `.cargo/config.toml` sets\n`RUST_TEST_THREADS = \"1\"` (and `run_all.sh` passes `--test-threads=1`); a wrong\ninvocation fails loudly with an explanatory message rather than flakily.\n`cargo test` also does not emit the `cdylib` artifact, so `cargo build` (or\n`run_all.sh`) must run first — the harness says so explicitly if the `.so` is\nmissing.\nEOF\nwc -l VERIFICATION.md","description":"Write VERIFICATION.md summary"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1980,"cache_read_input_tokens":318201,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1980,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d399b7ab-efa0-48e3-8602-3102beab604c","uuid":"1fb96c4b-f257-48e8-9cfa-2be19f333360","timestamp":"2026-08-19T20:58:46.208Z"}
